# React Flow render

Follow `packages/app/REACTFLOW_RENDER.md`. The App stays in the realignment as a client of the
host API; its graph renders **execution manifests (v2)**.

Non-negotiables:

- Published edges are **`data` or `route`**. Data edges come from `$ref` / `$state` (including
  nested paths) and from `expr` gates that read state, with handles. Route edges publish
  parallel / branch / loop structure. Strip unlabeled layout-control edges; never invent fake
  `$ref`s for structure.
- Do not emit `ecp-group` / `parentId` containers. Structure is shown with route connectors.
- Port bindings are literals, refs and `$expr` values; make sure output and nested input
  handles exist for every edged ref.
- Ports come from capabilities' JSON Schemas in plugin manifests, not from zod at run time.
- Fan-out through multiple `$ref`s is supported. Don't invent multi-source fan-in on one input
  key.
- Legacy `.when()` gates in v1 manifests map to `expr` in v2.
